---
import repositories from '../data/repositories.json';
const repos = repositories.filter(r => !r.fork && !r.private);
const featured = ['portop','auroraOS','pkgtui','termdock','qawk'];
const other = repos.filter(r => !featured.includes(r.name));
const repo = (name: string) => repos.find(r => r.name === name)!;
const stars = repos.reduce((n,r) => n+r.stargazers_count,0);
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"/>
<meta name="description" content="Luca Padovan — Platform & Senior Software Engineer in Bologna, Italy. Linux, embedded systems, platform engineering, and open-source developer tools."/>
<link rel="canonical" href="https://lucapadovan.dev/"/>
<meta property="og:title" content="Luca Padovan · Software Engineer"/><meta property="og:description" content="Linux systems. Useful tools. Open source. Explore the work of Luca Padovan."/><meta property="og:type" content="website"/><meta property="og:url" content="https://lucapadovan.dev/"/>
<meta name="theme-color" content="#111311"/><title>Luca Padovan · Software Engineer</title>
<link rel="icon" href="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 64 64'%3E%3Crect width='64' height='64' rx='14' fill='%23111311'/%3E%3Cpath d='m15 20 13 12-13 12M34 44h15' fill='none' stroke='%23c1f779' stroke-width='6'/%3E%3C/svg%3E"/>
</head>
<body>
<a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
<div class="page-shell">
<header><a class="wordmark" href="#" aria-label="Luca Padovan home"><span class="mark">&gt;_</span> LP<span class="muted"> / </span></a><nav aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="#projects">Projects</a><a href="#about">About</a><a href="#contact">Contact</a></nav><a class="header-gh" href="https://github.com/padovanl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a></header>
<main id="main">
<section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
<div class="hero-copy"><div class="eyebrow"><span>SOFTWARE ENGINEER</span><span class="location">BOLOGNA, ITALY</span></div>
<p class="hello">Hi, I'm Luca Padovan.</p><h1 id="hero-title">Close to the metal.<br/><span>Open to the world.</span></h1>
<p class="intro">I build Linux systems and tools that make a developer's day a little easier. From embedded platforms to open-source software, I like understanding how things work — and making them work better.</p>
<div class="hero-actions"><a class="button primary" href="#projects">Explore my projects</a><a class="button secondary" href="https://github.com/padovanl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Find me on GitHub</a></div>
<a class="linkedin-hero" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/lucapadovan/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Connect on LinkedIn</a><div class="hero-foot"><span>LINUX</span><span>EMBEDDED</span><span>PLATFORM ENGINEERING</span><span>OPEN SOURCE</span></div></div>
<aside class="terminal" aria-label="A short introduction in terminal form"><div class="terminal-title"><span class="window-dots" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span>luca@portfolio: ~</span><span class="term-end">bash</span></div><div class="terminal-content"><p><span class="prompt">❯</span> whoami</p><p class="output">Luca Padovan<br/>Platform & Senior Software Engineer</p><p><span class="prompt">❯</span> cat interests.txt</p><p class="output"><span class="lime">linux & embedded</span><br/>yocto · drivers · graphics<br/>OTA updates · CI/CD<br/>Go · Python · developer tools</p><p><span class="prompt">❯</span> ls ~/open-source</p><div class="terminal-repos"><a href="https://github.com/padovanl/portop">portop/</a><a href="https://github.com/padovanl/auroraOS">auroraOS/</a><a href="https://github.com/padovanl/pkgtui">pkgtui/</a><a href="https://github.com/padovanl/termdock">termdock/</a><a href="https://github.com/padovanl/qawk">qawk/</a></div><p class="last-line"><span class="prompt">❯</span> <span class="cursor" aria-hidden="true"></span></p></div><div class="terminal-bottom"><span>Built out of curiosity.</span><span>Shared as open source.</span></div></aside>
</section>
<div class="stat-strip"><div><strong data-total-repos>{repos.length}</strong><span>public repositories</span></div><div><strong data-total-stars>{stars}</strong><span>GitHub stars across my projects</span></div><div class="stat-text"><span class="small-label">THE COMMON THREAD</span><p>Practical software.<br/>A Linux state of mind.</p></div></div>
<section id="projects" class="projects section" aria-labelledby="projects-title"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">01 / SELECTED WORK</p><h2 id="projects-title">Made to be used.</h2></div><p>A few things I've built, maintained,<br class="desktop-break"/> and put out into the world.</p></div>
<div class="project-grid">
<article class="project featured-project"><div class="project-top"><span class="project-number">01</span><span class="badge">NETWORKING / GO</span><span class="repo-stars" data-stars="portop">☆ {repo('portop').stargazers_count}</span></div><div class="project-copy"><h3>portop<span class="name-dot">.</span></h3><p>What's really using your ports?</p><p class="description">An htop-style view of network ports and the processes behind them. Inspect systemd services and Docker containers in the terminal, web dashboard, or Cockpit.</p></div><a class="project-image" href="https://padovanl.github.io/portop/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Visit the Portop website"><img src="./assets/portop-dashboard.png" alt="Portop web dashboard showing network ports, processes, and services" width="1200" height="700" loading="lazy"/></a><div class="project-links"><a href="https://github.com/padovanl/portop" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Repository</a><a href="https://padovanl.github.io/portop/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Website & docs</a><span data-release="portop"></span></div></article>
<article class="project aurora-project"><div class="project-top"><span class="project-number">02</span><span class="badge">LINUX / DEBIAN</span><span class="repo-stars" data-stars="auroraOS">☆ {repo('auroraOS').stargazers_count}</span></div><div class="project-copy"><h3>Aurora OS<span class="name-dot">.</span></h3><p>A Linux desktop, with a fresh perspective.</p><p class="description">A developer-ready Debian distribution with a custom macOS-inspired desktop, built-in AI, snapshots, and everyday development tools.</p></div><a class="project-image" href="https://padovanl.github.io/auroraOS/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Visit the Aurora OS website"><img src="./assets/aurora-desktop.png" alt="The Aurora OS desktop with its custom interface and application dock" width="1200" height="700" loading="lazy"/></a><div class="project-links"><a href="https://github.com/padovanl/auroraOS" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Repository</a><a href="https://padovanl.github.io/auroraOS/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Website & docs</a><span data-release="auroraOS"></span></div></article>
<article class="project compact-project"><div class="project-top"><span class="project-number">03</span><span class="badge">PACKAGES / GO</span><span class="repo-stars" data-stars="pkgtui">☆ {repo('pkgtui').stargazers_count}</span></div><div class="project-copy"><div class="compact-symbol" aria-hidden="true">[pkg]</div><h3>pkgtui<span class="name-dot">.</span></h3><p>One terminal. Your package managers.</p><p class="description">Search, install, remove, and upgrade packages from APT, Snap, Flatpak, Homebrew, and MacPorts in one terminal interface.</p></div><div class="project-links"><a href="https://github.com/padovanl/pkgtui" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Repository</a><a href="https://github.com/padovanl/pkgtui#readme" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the docs</a><span data-release="pkgtui"></span></div></article>
<article class="project compact-project"><div class="project-top"><span class="project-number">04</span><span class="badge">TERMINAL / GO</span><span class="repo-stars" data-stars="termdock">☆ {repo('termdock').stargazers_count}</span></div><div class="project-copy"><div class="compact-symbol panes" aria-hidden="true">[ | ]</div><h3>termdock<span class="name-dot">.</span></h3><p>Your sessions, still running.</p><p class="description">A terminal multiplexer written from scratch in Go. Split panes, persistent sessions, detach and reattach — even from a different machine.</p></div><div class="project-links"><a href="https://github.com/padovanl/termdock" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Repository</a><a href="https://padovanl.github.io/termdock/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Website & docs</a><span data-release="termdock"></span></div></article>
<article class="project qawk-project"><div class="project-top"><span class="project-number">05</span><span class="badge">OTA / DEVICE FLEETS</span><span class="repo-stars" data-stars="qawk">☆ {repo('qawk').stargazers_count}</span></div><div class="qawk-layout"><div class="project-copy"><h3>qawk<span class="name-dot">.</span></h3><p>Updates that move together.</p><p class="description">A hawkBit-compatible OTA update server with release channels, staged rollouts, and multi-device orchestration. Built for managing releases across connected device fleets.</p></div><div class="qawk-capabilities"><span class="small-label">RELEASE MANAGEMENT</span><div><span>Release channels</span><span>Staged rollouts</span><span>Device orchestration</span><span>hawkBit compatibility</span></div></div></div><div class="project-links"><a href="https://github.com/padovanl/qawk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Repository</a><a href="https://github.com/padovanl/qawk#readme" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the docs</a><span data-release="qawk"></span></div></article></div>
<details class="archive"><summary><span>More from the workbench</span><span class="archive-count">{other.length} more repositories</span><span class="expand" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="archive-list" data-repo-list>{other.map(r=><a href={r.html_url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span>{r.name}</span><span class="archive-description">{r.description || (r.language ? `${r.language} project` : 'Explore the repository')}</span><span class="archive-language">{r.language || 'Code'}</span></a>)}</div></details>
<p class="data-note" data-data-note>Repository snapshot: October 3, 2026. Stars and releases refresh from GitHub when available.</p>
</section>
<section class="about section" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">02 / BEHIND THE CODE</p><div class="portrait"><img src="./assets/luca-padovan.jpg" alt="Luca Padovan" width="400" height="400" loading="lazy"/></div><h2 id="about-title">Systems thinker.<br/>Hands-on builder.</h2><div class="about-location"><span class="coordinate">44.49° N / 11.34° E</span><span>Bologna, Italy</span></div></div><div class="about-copy"><p class="about-lead">I'm a Platform & Senior Software Engineer at QubicaAMF, working across Linux, embedded systems, and the software infrastructure behind bowling and entertainment systems.</p><p>My work spans Yocto-based operating systems, embedded applications, Linux drivers and graphics, OTA updates, recovery, logging, and monitoring. I also manage CI/CD infrastructure, containers, orchestration, and observability, with a focus on cost and operational efficiency.</p><p>I coordinate multiple project streams and external consultants, connecting hands-on engineering with the wider architecture and delivery of a platform.</p><p>Outside work, I build open-source projects out of curiosity and a love of coding. Often, they start with a small everyday annoyance: a port I can't identify, too many package-manager commands, or a terminal session I don't want to lose.</p><div class="work-focus"><div><span>01</span><p><strong>Embedded Linux</strong>Yocto builds, system integration, drivers, and graphics.</p></div><div><span>02</span><p><strong>Platform & delivery</strong>CI/CD infrastructure and repeatable build workflows.</p></div><div><span>03</span><p><strong>Software updates</strong>OTA strategies and device update lifecycles.</p></div></div><div class="expertise"><span>Software design</span><span>Linux & Yocto</span><span>C / C++</span><span>Docker</span><span>Kubernetes</span><span>Observability</span><span>Embedded systems</span><span>OTA updates</span><span>CI/CD</span><span>Go</span><span>Python</span><span>Open source</span></div></div></section>
<section class="experience section" id="experience" aria-labelledby="experience-title"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">03 / EXPERIENCE</p><h2 id="experience-title">From firmware to platforms.</h2></div><p>A path through embedded systems,<br class="desktop-break"/> software, and infrastructure.</p></div><div class="career-list"><article><div class="career-date">FEB 2024 — PRESENT</div><div><h3>QubicaAMF</h3><p class="career-role">Platform & Senior Software Engineer</p><p>Embedded Linux platforms and system infrastructure, from operating-system customization to updates, recovery, logging, and monitoring. CI/CD, containers, orchestration, observability, cost optimization, and coordination of consultants and project streams.</p></div></article><article><div class="career-date">MAY 2023 — FEB 2024</div><div><h3>QubicaAMF</h3><p class="career-role">Senior Software Engineer</p><p>Software infrastructure and embedded Linux applications for bowling and entertainment systems, including system customization and operational services.</p></div></article><article><div class="career-date">JUL 2021 — MAY 2023</div><div><h3>HiFuture · Teoresi Group</h3><p class="career-role">Software Engineer</p><p>WinForms and WPF human-machine interfaces for biomedical and microelectronics applications, with software requirements specifications and test plans.</p></div></article><article><div class="career-date">APR 2019 — JUL 2021</div><div><h3>T3LAB</h3><p class="career-role">Software & Firmware Engineer</p><p>C/C++ applications, deployment, and functional testing on ARM multicore SoCs running embedded Linux. Open-source cloud infrastructure with OpenStack, PackStack, Kubernetes, and federated authentication for the SBDIO I4.0 project.</p></div></article><article><div class="career-date">OCT 2018 — MAR 2019</div><div><h3>Datalogic</h3><p class="career-role">Student Internship</p><p>Master's thesis work on “Machine Learning Platforms for Mobile Computing”.</p></div></article></div><div class="education-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">EDUCATION</p><h3>University of Ferrara</h3><p>Master's degree in Computer and Automation Engineering <span>2016–2018</span></p><p>Bachelor's degree in Computer and Electronic Engineering <span>2012–2016</span></p></div><div><p class="eyebrow">CERTIFICATIONS & TRAINING</p><ul><li>Embedded Linux Development · LDF450</li><li>PCAP · Certified Associate in Python Programming</li><li>CPA · C++ Certified Associate Programmer</li><li>Embedded Linux and Yocto Project course</li></ul></div></div></section><section class="contact section" id="contact" aria-labelledby="contact-title"><p class="eyebrow">04 / KEEP IN TOUCH</p><div class="contact-row"><div><h2 id="contact-title">Good software starts<br/>with a conversation.</h2><p>Have a question, an idea, or a shared interest?<br/>Let's talk on LinkedIn, or build something on GitHub.</p></div><div class="contact-actions"><a class="button primary" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/lucapadovan/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Connect on LinkedIn</a><a class="button secondary" href="https://github.com/padovanl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore my GitHub</a></div></div></section>
</main><footer><span>© {new Date().getFullYear()} Luca Padovan</span><span>Built with Astro. Fueled by curiosity.</span><a href="#main">Back to top</a></footer>
</div><script is:inline src="./live.js" defer></script>
</body></html>
<style is:global>
